compare/tip/translate.test.ts:
(pass) structural index witnesses preserve TIP evaluation at random goals and function arguments [25.52ms]
(pass) a structural index witness is proven by the kernel, not assumed [7391.63ms]
(pass) witness substitution is simultaneous and avoids let, match and lambda capture [0.32ms]
(pass) index synthesis uses datatype shape, field order and fresh names, not benchmark names [0.62ms]
(pass) abstract sorts: the claim at every sort, proven or refuted as TIP states it [787.88ms]
(pass) function variables into a list and lambdas: told apart, as TIP states them [4008.13ms]
(pass) what stays outside is refused with its reason [0.33ms]

research/security/mutants/mutants.test.ts:
(pass) all owned modules receive only one-site generic mutations and keep every stated law [33.42ms]
(pass) renaming and formatting do not select different operators; constructors are not operation guards [0.66ms]
(pass) policy replay checks the prerequisite before the call, and refuses unknown syntax or names [1.24ms]
(pass) old and new map domains detect foreign insertion and deleting a foreign zero-valued row [0.36ms]
(pass) trace arguments are parsed as literals, not evaluated as code [1.01ms]
(pass) detection needs both readable sides, a matching stated refutation and two successful source replays [0.15ms]
(pass) stated policies match the public security templates [0.46ms]
(pass) a real violation in another method is not a replay of the scoped step law [1.90ms]
(pass) read isolation compares intermediate observations, not only an equal final result [3.95ms]
(pass) source scheduling hooks stay outside locks and transactions; operators expose the intended boundaries [3.52ms]
(pass) source races also reproduce with native runtime preemption and no scheduling hooks [1237.50ms]
(pass) the complete saved corpus replays without asking the prover again [123.44ms]
